Hey Phil,

using your package I became aware of some odd behavior of the mirt-function.

By coincidence I realized that the results change depending on the order of items within the data set.

Here is a simple example of what I mean:

data <- expand.table(LSAT7)

mod1 <- mirt(data,2)

mod2 <- mirt(data[2,4,3,1,5],2)

However, mod1 and mod 2 are not equivalent. How can this be?

Regards,

Kornelius

